# build output
dist/
.output/
.vercel/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# macOS-specific files
.DS_Store

# CloudFlare
.wrangler/

# Database ORM
# Note: no trailing slash. The drizzle configs load this FILE (scripts/drizzle-config.ts) and it
# holds CLOUDFLARE_D1_API_TOKEN; `.drizzle.env/` would only match a directory and leave the
# token committable.
.drizzle.env

# Astro
.astro/

# svelte-check's incremental cache: a derived tsconfig, the svelte2tsx mirror of every .svelte and
# tsbuildinfo.json. `npm run check:svelte` (D288) regenerates it; committing it would freeze a snapshot of a
# compiler's intermediate output beside the source it came from.
.svelte-check/

# Skill installs regenerate this mirror of .agents/skills for other agent CLIs.
.hermes/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars

# Content placeholders. `src/content.local/` holds build-time overlays of `src/content.json` used to make a
# REVIEW build (measured shot-cards in the reserved photo places). Only `src/content.local.example.json` is
# tracked: nothing tracked may switch a placeholder on, and scripts/check-content.mjs fails any built page
# carrying a `data-placeholder` fill, so a review-only state cannot reach the apex the way .dev.vars cannot
# leak a secret. A DIRECTORY, deliberately: `import.meta.glob('../content.local.json')` was measured to also
# match `content.local.example.json`, which would have made the tracked example the override.
src/content.local/

# Local database files
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# API keys and secrets
*.pem
*.key

# Dev Notes
.notes/

# Context-handoff records written by the pi-context-budget extension when a session's context is
# reset (see .notes/runbooks/context-handoff-budget.md). They are session state, not site content.
.ai-work/

# Design pass. The durable half is TRACKED in `design/` (no dot): the gates and their harness, the
# probes behind every number DESIGN.md quotes, the specimens, the machine records — see
# design/README.md and design/records/0009-design-evidence-is-tracked.md.
# `.design/` (with the dot) is scratch, so the WHOLE directory is ignored (D286): candidate font binaries
# (re-fetchable from @fontsource), the render gate's raw per-run numbers, `tmp-*` dumps, the operator's
# Meetup source figure (Meetup's images are not ours to republish on another domain —
# .notes/asset-sources.md — the reading of them is tracked, in DESIGN.md's mark rules and D126),
# hand-kept snapshots of source files (a copy here is inert: the build reads `src/`, so a stale one is a
# trap), and ad hoc measurement dumps. The durable form of any number worth keeping is a JSON under
# `design/` that a script writes and a doc cites.
# An earlier version of this block named four patterns and went stale the day a probe wrote PNGs into
# `.design/rsvp-shot/`: a per-pattern list is a promise every new probe has to remember, and an unignored
# scratch file shows up in `git status` as a candidate commit. The tracked artifact is the script, never
# the pixels.
# The three basename patterns below are NOT redundant with `.design/`: page-measure/probe write
# .probe-shot-<w>.png, .measured-*.html and rendered-*.html NEXT TO whatever they probe, which can be a
# specimen inside design/ — so they carry no leading directory, which keeps both directories clean.
.design/
.probe-shot-*.png
.measured-*.html
rendered-*.html

# Machine-local pi agent state: a local-model endpoint (and its key) can land
# here, so it is host-specific like durig.config.json and never committed.
.pi/
